%% Title: Sequence · POST /api/refresh
%% Summary: How an on-demand collection is requested: the same-origin guard, the shared-secret check, the in-flight and debounce guards, the 202 hand-off to the worker, and the worker completing the job row.
%% Sources: src/routes/refresh.js, src/middleware/same-origin.js, src/server.js (mount order, no CORS), src/queues/index.js (collect.refresh), src/workers/collect.worker.js (processRefreshJob), src/collectors/runner.js, src/db/migrations/019_refresh_inflight.sql. Spec: TECHNICAL_SPEC.md section 7 (POST /api/refresh) and section 8 (rate limiting). The page itself never calls this endpoint.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Caller as Caller (browser tab or script)
  participant Web as web · refresh router (no CORS)
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant Q as Redis · collect.refresh
  participant W as worker · processRefreshJob
  participant Src as registry sources

  opt CORS preflight
    Caller->>Web: OPTIONS /api/refresh
    Web-->>Caller: 403, no Access-Control-Allow-* headers
  end
  Caller->>Web: POST /api/refresh
  Web->>Web: requireSameOrigin: Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin or none,<br/>without it, Origin (else Referer) host = Host header
  alt cross-site or unprovable
    Web-->>Caller: 403 Cross-site request rejected
  end
  Web->>Web: REFRESH_TOKEN set → X-Refresh-Token must match (timing-safe),<br/>unset but PULSE_BIND_ADDR / HOST beyond loopback → refused
  alt token missing or wrong
    Web-->>Caller: 403
  end
  Web->>DB: mark 'api' jobs running longer than REFRESH_STALE_MINUTES (30) failed
  Web->>DB: SELECT a running 'api' job
  alt one is running
    Web-->>Caller: 409 with its job_id
  end
  alt another refresh accepted in the last 60 s (global, in-process)
    Web-->>Caller: 429 with Retry-After
  end
  Web->>DB: INSERT processing_jobs (triggered_by api, status running)
  alt unique index uq_processing_jobs_api_running (migration 019) rejects it
    Web-->>Caller: 409 with the other job_id
  end
  Web->>Q: add collect-all { jobId }
  alt queue unavailable
    Web->>DB: job failed, debounce budget not spent
    Web-->>Caller: 503 Collection queue unavailable
  end
  Web-->>Caller: 202 { job_id, status: queued, triggered_by: api }

  Q->>W: collect-all job (concurrency 1)
  W->>DB: job still running? else skip
  W->>Src: runCollection over every registry source<br/>(same gates, claim and guards as a scheduled run)
  W->>DB: raw_posts, scores, audit rows, source_runs
  W->>DB: bias checks for the job when it stored new posts, then completed<br/>with genuine counts (or awaiting_retries until reserved scoring retries finish)
